{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1043842-fantastic-beasts-and-how-to-build-them-a-request-for-help","id":1043842,"title":"Fantastic Beasts and how to Build Them (A Request for Help)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-04T20:43:24-08:00","id":1043842,"title":"Fantastic Beasts and how to Build Them (A Request for Help)","content":"The application of the Life Arcanum to create replicas of existing creatures is well documented, and easily done within the rules.<br /> Just grab yourself a copy of Blood and Smoke, and enjoy your new Dog, Wolf, Elephant, Horse, or whatever.<br /> Even slightly more radical, but still quite simple modifications can be easily made, such as a Dog with Gills, or (for whatever reason) a Squirrel with Tentacles.<br /> But when you start to build creatures from outside of the normal realms of possibility, such as Dragons, Goblins, or even 3-headed 6-legged armour plated turbo-phants, you start to lose all direction.<br /> <br /> How do you stat such a creature? In many cases, it'll be a mere plot contrivance, your creation smashes the door down, or crushes the Gulmoth underfoot, or whathaveyou.<br /> But when you use Magic to become such a creature, and face down your enemies in a terrifying scaly, clawed, draconic form, how do you determine what is reasonable?<br /> Players will want to know exactly what their new Strength is. What the species factor is for their movement.<br /> <br /> This might seem like a question with no answer, but I'm holding out in hope that someone else has asked this before, and decided that he'll build the stats for Dragon, or so forth.<br /> Also merely saying that such a thing wouldn't work isn't exactly feasible. With a Rote, it's very easy to turn your ferocious pet Dog into a 3m tall war-beast with terrifying fangs without Paradox, for a few seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T14:11:26-08:00","id":1044167,"title":"","content":"I would love to see what people come up with here.<br /> <br /> Night Horrors: Grim Fears is a pretty good book for fantastical creatures.<br /> <br /> Here's the <b>Dragon</b> from it:<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 7, Wits: 5, Resolve: 10<br /> Strength: 20, Dex: 5, Stamina: 20<br /> Presence: 12, Manipulation: 7, Composure: 9<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Initiative: +14<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Speed: 30<br /> Health: 40<br /> Armor: 7 (immune to modern Firearms)<br /> Claw: 1L (31 dice)<br /> Bite: 2L (32 dice)<br /> Breath Weapon: 0A (8 dice cone attack)<br /> <br /> This was a 1e creature, btw. It also had a bunch of Glamour related powers as well.<br /> <br /> You could tone down it's mental and social stats and replace those with a player character's.<br /> <br /> I think a good basis for a balanced <b>Dragon template</b> would be:<br /> <br /> Strength: +8, Dex: +3, Stamina: +8, Size: 15 (and all derived stats from there)<br /> Claw: 1L (strength + brawl)<br /> Bite: 2L (strength + brawl)<br /> Breath Weapon: 3L (gnosis + life, gnosis x 5 cone base)<br /> Armor: 5<br /> <br /> So a typical Mage with Gnosis 5 &amp; Life 5 would become:<br /> <br /> Strength: 10, Dex: 5, Stamina: 10, Size 15, Health 25<br /> Claw: 1L (12 dice)<br /> Bite: 1L (12 dice)<br /> Breath Weapon: 3L (10 dice, 25 foot cone)<br /> Armor: 5<br /> <br /> That seems pretty scary to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 02-05-2017, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}